{"contract_version":5,"artifact":"weekly-cases","statement":"Model projections from reported counts, not predictions of what will happen. Each of 1000 ensemble members draws one reproduction number from its posterior over the last 3 complete weeks and projects weekly counts 8 weeks ahead with Poisson noise, holding that number constant; the bands are quantiles of the members. A series with fewer than 11 cases in those weeks is not forecast. Every forecast describes cases under its own case definition and never mixes definitions.","method":"Renewal-equation projection (Nouvellet P, Cori A, Garske T, et al. A simple approach to measure transmissibility and forecast incidence. Epidemics 2018;22:29-35, doi:10.1016/j.epidem.2017.02.012; RECON projections package). R is the Cori et al. 2013 posterior over the last 3 weeks ending at the origin week; each member's counts follow Poisson(R times the infectivity from the measles serial interval), observed counts before the origin and the member's own after it. There is no overdispersion, importation, seasonality or vaccination in this model.","origin_week":{"year":2026,"week":36},"latest_data_week":{"year":2026,"week":38},"origin_rule":"The origin week is the latest week with a row in the input (MMWR 2026-W38) less its 2 most recent weeks, which are provisional because of reporting delay (the same rule as the published R_t, spec E5). Nothing after the origin week is read.","horizon_weeks":8,"run_count":1000,"seed":20250101,"levels":[0.01,0.025,0.05,0.1,0.15,0.2,0.25,0.3,0.35,0.4,0.45,0.5,0.55,0.6,0.65,0.7,0.75,0.8,0.85,0.9,0.95,0.975,0.99],"input":{"artifact":"weekly-cases","sha256":"6bb73ec0a2b22585cb02b64c544b65b30630dd277221cdc36abc181cfde7363e","rows":6844},"parameters":[{"parameter":"window_weeks","value":3,"source":"This project's pre-registered rule, fixed before any backtest score (koplik_epi::forecast::ForecastConfig::DEFAULT_WINDOW_WEEKS)","url":null,"note":"Three weeks is about 1.8 mean measles serial intervals, so the window spans at least one generation of infectors and infectees while staying short enough to follow a change within a month. Not taken from the cited paper; never varied against a score (the backtest report lists windows 1, 2 and 4 beside it)."},{"parameter":"max_lag_weeks","value":3,"source":"This project's pre-registered rule: the smallest look-back whose dropped serial-interval mass is under 1%, the tolerance koplik_epi::rt documents for its own truncation","url":null,"note":"Measured for the measles serial interval: 6.6% dropped with a 2-week look-back, 0.54% with 3. A longer look-back would postpone the first week a forecast can be made from a series that starts mid-outbreak."},{"parameter":"min_cases","value":11,"source":"Cori A, Ferguson NM, Fraser C, Cauchemez S. Am J Epidemiol 2013;178(9):1505-1512, Web Appendix 2; EpiEstim estimate_R.R: ceiling(1 / cv_posterior^2 - a_prior) with cv_posterior 0.3","url":"https://doi.org/10.1093/aje/kwt133","note":"Fewer cases than this in the estimation window gives insufficient_data and no forecast, never a prior-driven number."},{"parameter":"prior_mean","value":5.0,"source":"EpiEstim make_config.R default mean_prior = 5, as in Cori et al. 2013","url":"https://doi.org/10.1093/aje/kwt133","note":"Gamma prior on the reproduction number R; with at least min_cases cases in the window the data dominate it."},{"parameter":"prior_sd","value":5.0,"source":"EpiEstim make_config.R default std_prior = 5, as in Cori et al. 2013","url":"https://doi.org/10.1093/aje/kwt133","note":"Gamma prior on the reproduction number R."},{"parameter":"serial_interval_mean_days","value":11.7,"source":"CDC, Nowcasting to Estimate Real-Time Measles Transmission Trends, MMWR 2026;75(33) (mm7533a1), citing Klinkenberg D, Nishiura H. J Theor Biol 2011;284:52-60; Vink MA, Bootsma MCJ, Wallinga J. Am J Epidemiol 2014;180(9):865-875","url":"https://www.cdc.gov/mmwr/volumes/75/wr/mm7533a1.htm","note":"Gamma-distributed serial interval, discretised to MMWR weeks. CDC's figure is a generation interval; the serial interval is used as its observable proxy, with the same mean."},{"parameter":"serial_interval_sd_days","value":3.0,"source":"CDC MMWR 2026;75(33): variance of 9 days squared","url":"https://www.cdc.gov/mmwr/volumes/75/wr/mm7533a1.htm","note":"Standard deviation of the gamma serial interval."},{"parameter":"horizon_weeks","value":8,"source":"Koplik spec, Principle question 4: a 4-8 week outbreak forecast","url":null,"note":"The far end of the stated range, so every horizon from 1 to 8 is published."},{"parameter":"run_count","value":1000,"source":"Koplik spec E4: a 1,000-run simulated ensemble","url":null,"note":"The 1% and 99% quantiles rest on about ten members each."},{"parameter":"quantile_levels","value":[0.01,0.025,0.05,0.1,0.15,0.2,0.25,0.3,0.35,0.4,0.45,0.5,0.55,0.6,0.65,0.7,0.75,0.8,0.85,0.9,0.95,0.975,0.99],"source":"The 23 quantile levels of the CDC FluSight / hubverse format; Bracher J, Ray EL, Gneiting T, Reich NG. PLoS Comput Biol 2021;17(2):e1008618","url":"https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pcbi.1008618","note":"Includes the 50% (0.25, 0.75) and 90% (0.05, 0.95) central intervals the backtest scored. Quantiles are Hyndman-Fan type 7 of the member counts."},{"parameter":"seed","value":20250101,"source":"An arbitrary fixed constant chosen before any run; the backtest's base seed","url":null,"note":"Changes only the Monte Carlo draw, never the model. Members derive their own seeds from it, the geography and the member index."},{"parameter":"provisional_weeks","value":2,"source":"Koplik spec E5: the most recent two weeks are provisional (reporting delay); the same rule as the published R_t","url":null,"note":"These weeks are not read: the origin week is the latest week with a row, less this many weeks."}],"series":[{"geography":"01","case_definition":"confirmed_or_unknown_status","status":"insufficient_data","reason":"below_threshold","cases_in_window":0,"skill":"not backtested; no measured skill"},{