ill":"not backtested; no measured skill"},{"geography":"48397","case_definition":"confirmed","status":"insufficient_data","reason":"missing_count","cases_in_window":null,"skill":"not backtested; no measured skill"},{"geography":"48445","case_definition":"confirmed","status":"insufficient_data","reason":"missing_count","cases_in_window":null,"skill":"not backtested; no measured skill"},{"geography":"48459","case_definition":"confirmed","status":"insufficient_data","reason":"missing_count","cases_in_window":null,"skill":"not backtested; no measured skill"},{"geography":"48501","case_definition":"confirmed","status":"insufficient_data","reason":"missing_count","cases_in_window":null,"skill":"not backtested; no measured skill"}],"backtest":{"name":"the 2025 West Texas outbreak","series":"Texas DSHS outbreak total (all outbreak-associated confirmed cases, every county combined), weekly by report date","geography":"48","case_definition":"confirmed","protocol":"real-time by report vintage: at each forecast date only versions with first_seen_at <= the date are used; truth is the final series from every version","seed":20250101,"targets":48,"forecast_dates":7,"origin_weeks":5,"mean_crps":3.6569772499999993,"coverage_50":0.4791666666666667,"coverage_90":0.625,"mean_persistence_abs_error":5.791666666666667,"by_horizon":[{"horizon":1,"n":7,"mean_crps":2.8310717142857142,"coverage_50":0.2857142857142857,"coverage_90":0.42857142857142855},{"horizon":2,"n":7,"mean_crps":3.857115571428572,"coverage_50":0.5714285714285714,"coverage_90":0.7142857142857143},{"horizon":3,"n":7,"mean_crps":5.026302571428572,"coverage_50":0.14285714285714285,"coverage_90":0.42857142857142855},{"horizon":4,"n":7,"mean_crps":6.655408857142857,"coverage_50":0.5714285714285714,"coverage_90":0.5714285714285714},{"horizon":5,"n":5,"mean_crps":2.370539,"coverage_50":0.4,"coverage_90":0.8},{"horizon":6,"n":5,"mean_crps":1.9078392,"coverage_50":0.6,"coverage_90":0.8},{"horizon":7,"n":5,"mean_crps":3.3611994000000003,"coverage_50":0.6,"coverage_90":0.6},{"horizon":8,"n":5,"mean_crps":1.7495458000000004,"coverage_50":0.8,"coverage_90":0.8}],"report_path":"data/reports/backtest/west-texas-2025.json","report_sha256":"af8d6143905be29bcdff9953cd5ef0e965207d65e023ce0b4b9b01f4300d45cd","manifest_sha256":"00ce05dd4730969da533bf1de684f07db8ae9485785912d28a9007f4f2b90a25","limitations":["One series and one period: Texas DSHS outbreak total (all outbreak-associated confirmed cases, every county combined), weekly by report date; no county-level backtest (county breakdowns are unavailable for 2025-03-28..2025-08-12, Issue #1402). No state series, county series or other outbreak was scored.","A small sample: 48 scored targets from 7 forecast dates, which come from 5 distinct origin weeks (a forecast date whose latest complete week had not advanced repeats the previous forecast, so those origins count twice).","Small counts: the 48 weekly counts the forecasts were scored against ran from 0 to 10 cases. The score is in cases, so it depends on the size of the series and is not comparable with a series of a different size.","In this backtest the intervals were not well calibrated: 90% intervals contained the observed count 62.5% (30 of 48) of the time (nominal 90%) and 50% intervals 47.9% (23 of 48) (nominal 50%). The model has no overdispersion, which under-states the spread of real measles clusters.","Counts are by report date, not symptom onset: they say when the source published the cases."]},"scope_note":"The backtest scored one series only: Texas DSHS outbreak total (all outbreak-associated confirmed cases, every county combined), weekly by report date. None of the 6 series forecast here is that series: none was backtested and none has a measured skill. Its scores are reported separately, as an evaluation of the method on that series, and are not a measure of the forecasts of any other series."}
